From 707704835daac7515c8899cfb3090f08aabce0e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kazhiramatsu <kazutakehiramatsu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 14:52:53 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix(emitter): name anonymous classes in decorated computed
 fields by the hoisted key

visitPropertyDeclaration (_tsc.js 100041) runs the named evaluation of an
anonymous decorated class initializer before the element work:
getAssignedNameOfPropertyName hoists `getGeneratedNameForNode(name)` in the
class IIFE environment and rewrites the name to `[_a = __propKey(expression)]`
with the key expression unvisited; the class receives `__setFunctionName(this,
_a)`. partialTransformClassElement then reaches visitReferencedPropertyName
with that rewritten name, whose second getGeneratedNameForNode resolves to the
same cached name (getNodeForGeneratedName walks `original`) and whose
hoistVariableDeclaration declares it again: `var _a, _a`, and the assignment
is wrapped once more, `_a = __propKey(_a = __propKey(fieldKey))`, before the
pending decorator assignment is injected.

The Rust named evaluation returned early for decorated members (an open row).
It now hands the rewritten name, its cache assignment and the hoisted binding
to the property plan; visit_referenced_property_name declares the same binding
again (`hoist_existing_temp_variable`, no temp ordinal advance) instead of
allocating a second one, visits the assignment under the name frame and wraps
it. Undecorated members keep the previsit path.

Focused witnesses: anonymous-in-decorated-computed-field x6 and
named-in-decorated-computed-field-control x6 exact twice, exit 0
(ratchets/h2-8a-decorator-followup-cause2-focused.v1.json).
---
 .../src/builtins/standard_decorators.rs       | 135 ++++++++++++++----
 ...-decorator-followup-cause2-focused.v1.json | 124 ++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 230 insertions(+), 29 deletions(-)
